  "summary": "Malicious code in aasp-tent-aasp-tent-core (npm)",
  "details": "On require(), the package detects the host OS and architecture (Windows, Linux x64/arm64, macOS), then downloads a platform-specific binary from one of three Cloudflare Workers endpoints (oob-worker[.]cf101-adf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev) over HTTPS, with a DNS TXT-record-based fallback using domains tin[.]dl[.]well1[.]site, tina[.]dl[.]well1[.]site, ldr[.]dl[.]well1[.]site, and win[.]dl[.]well1[.]site. The downloaded binary is written to /var/tmp/.cache_\u003crandom_hex\u003e (or %TEMP%\\dotnet_diag_\u003crandom_hex\u003e.exe on Windows), made executable, and spawned as a detached background process with stdio ignored. A marker file at /tmp/.analytics_state (or %TEMP%\\analytics_state) prevents re-execution within a window. The package has no repository, no lifecycle hooks, and its stated purpose as a \"platform core\" is inconsistent with the binary downloader behaviour.",
  "affected": [
    {
      "package": {
        "ecosystem": "npm",
        "name": "aasp-tent-aasp-tent-core",
        "purl": "pkg:npm/aasp-tent-aasp-tent-core@0.0.2"
      },
